on or  succumbing to insanity and ultimately  ends up destroying herself and those  around her so there aren't any surprises  really as far as the plot goes but it's  still like a really wild and very grimly  entertaining ride even though you know  like i said it's almost kind of like  watching like a slow motion car crash  like you know that it's gonna happen but  it's just kind of like you can't do  anything to stop it and you're just like  sit there sitting there like powerless  and you're just like watching it like in  horrified fascination it's kind of like  that um so i absolutely wouldn't  hesitate to recommend this to anyone  who's into psychological horror  possession horror  it does have something of a literary  fiction bent if you want to call it that  but  not so much in the writing style like i  said it's very uh matter of fact it's  very conversational because it's in the  first person so you're pretty much  inside amanda's head pretty much the  entire time so it's not real highfalutin  or anything like that it's just very  visceral it's very straightforward and i  think that really really works a lot to  its advantage and makes it  that much more entertaining and more  horrifying because you're seeing  everything from her perspective and  you're not entirely sure like you can  see how her life is spiraling out of  control and you can't really do anything  to stop her to help it and i think that  helper and i think that's like really  really uh scary and it's really really  entertaining at the same time so that  will do it for this uh tomes of terror  as i mentioned this book is available on  kindle unlimited uh so if you have  kindle unlimited you can read it for  free it's very short less than 200 pages  so you should probably like be able to  finish it off in an afternoon because  it's a really really fun read as well so  uh yeah that'll do it for this one i  will see you guys on the next one bye

